WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.102
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 9: Lights, Camera, Action…

2
00:00:04.182 --> 00:00:10.623
Unit 9 is about scripts: the writing that actors
follow on a stage and in front of a camera.

3
00:00:10.703 --> 00:00:16.718
You will read “The Forest Guardians” first
as a play script and then as a film script,

4
00:00:16.798 --> 00:00:22.459
comparing stage directions with camera
directions such as pan, zoom and close-up.

5
00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:27.846
You will also study compound nouns like
woodland, footpath and bamboo grove,

6
00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:31.248
and write and perform a short scene of your own.

7
00:00:31.328 --> 00:00:34.651
The unit story, “Nookwatch: The Forest Mission”,

8
00:00:34.731 --> 00:00:40.817
follows Amal and Sami as they help rescue
an injured lemur at a woodland rescue centre.

9
00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:46.771
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:53.311
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
recognise the layout and features of a play script,

11
00:00:53.391 --> 00:00:58.761
including the cast list, character names,
colons, dialogue and stage directions.

12
00:00:58.841 --> 00:01:04.006
You will also explain the difference
between a play script and a film script,

13
00:01:04.086 --> 00:01:08.094
using examples from both versions of “The Forest Guardians”.

14
00:01:08.174 --> 00:01:13.339
You will also read stage directions
accurately and locate upstage, downstage,

15
00:01:13.419 --> 00:01:17.086
centre stage and the entrances and exits they describe.

16
00:01:17.166 --> 00:01:19.607
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:01:19.687 --> 00:01:25.533
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
nook, woodland, bamboo, groove, fertile, textbook.

18
00:01:25.613 --> 00:01:30.533
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:30.613 --> 00:01:34.423
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:34.503 --> 00:01:40.070
The reading sequence includes The Forest
Guardians: a play script and The Forest Guardians:

21
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.056
the same scene as a film script.

22
00:01:42.136 --> 00:01:42.925
Read actively.

23
00:01:43.005 --> 00:01:47.207
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:47.287 --> 00:01:51.241
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:01:51.321 --> 00:01:54.886
The first language focus is What a Compound Noun Is.

26
00:01:54.966 --> 00:02:00.775
A compound noun joins two or more words so
that together they name one single thing.

27
00:02:00.855 --> 00:02:07.225
Knowing the parts lets you work out a new word
without reaching for a dictionary every time.

28
00:02:07.305 --> 00:02:14.866
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:14.946 --> 00:02:19.057
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Read the Script Aloud.

30
00:02:19.137 --> 00:02:23.377
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:23.457 --> 00:02:26.666
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.083
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:30.163 --> 00:02:31.678
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:31.758 --> 00:02:38.542
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:38.622 --> 00:02:41.870
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:49.704
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
